================================================================================
Robot model assets (redistributed in UGClient builds)
================================================================================

UGClient builds include robot description files (URDF), Draco-compressed visual
meshes (GLB), kinematics YAML and runtime configuration taken, at build time,
from ufactory_genesis (https://github.com/xArm-Developer/ufactory_genesis,
MIT License, pinned commit recorded in core/pyproject.toml). These files are
derivatives modified by ufactory_genesis; UGClient redistributes them unchanged
and does not vendor them in this git repository.

Attribution, as stated in the ufactory_genesis NOTICE:

  Robot description files and mesh assets under `assets/urdf/` include material
  derived from upstream UFACTORY / xArm ROS packages. Those assets are **not**
  pure original MIT-only content.

  xArm / UF850 / Lite6 URDF and meshes
  - Upstream: xArm-Developer/xarm_ros2 (https://github.com/xArm-Developer/xarm_ros2)
    (and related xArm ROS description packages historically used to generate
    standalone URDFs in this tree).
  - Typical upstream license: BSD-3-Clause (see the upstream repository's
    LICENSE / package metadata; a full copy is not vendored here).
  - This repository's modifications include (non-exhaustive):
    - Standalone URDF layouts and combo URDFs for Genesis (arm + end-effector).
    - Collision mesh packaging and visual GLB conversion / Draco compression.
    - Shared visual_glb/ layouts and link-canonical gripper visuals.
    - Runtime manifests, overlays, and integrity budgets used by tests.

  End-effectors (Gripper G2, Bio Gripper G2, Lite6 Gripper, Lite6 Vacuum)
  Visual and collision meshes for accessories follow the same upstream family
  where noted in each assets/urdf/<name>/README.md. Combo URDFs, movable
  visual variants, and compressed GLBs are maintained in that repository.

The full ufactory_genesis NOTICE is shipped alongside the assets in every build
(robot-assets/NOTICE.ufactory_genesis and the sidecar's NOTICE file).

